# Legacy Symbol Migration In Argdown+

[S1]: Carbon pricing reduces emissions.

[S2]: Lower emissions reduce climate risk.

[S3]: Transition costs can be mitigated by rebates.

[A1]: Incentive argument for pricing.
  +> [S1]

[S1]
  + [S2]
  -> [S3]: Some sectors face short-term transition costs.

[S2]
  >< [S4]: Emissions reductions do not lower climate risk.

[S4]: Climate risk remains unchanged.

[S5]: Canada's rebate-backed carbon pricing system is a concrete example.

[S2]
  ~= [S2-Alt]: Lower emissions reduce expected climate harms.

